/-
# Theorem V_odd: the direct certificates (PROOF_VODD §0, §3)

`exists_certOdd_proof`: at each of the 11 traces of `certA` a `DualCertU a` with `Φ ≤ PhiC a`.

**Departure from PROOF_VODD's certificates** (`handoff/log2log3/pilot_za/lean_certza/`, which produced `PhiC` in the
per-cell-maximum format of `Cert/Instance.lean`, at grids up to `L = 3200`): the certificates here are in the
linear-majorant format (`Cert/Lin.lean`, `Cert/LinInstance.lean`; data and kernel checks in `VOdd/CertData/A*.lean`,
generated by `scripts/gen_cert_lin.py`), on much coarser grids (`L = 20 … 100`), with rational exponents
`PhiQ < PhiC a`; a `DualCertU a` with `Φ ≤ PhiC a` is then obtained by refining the grid (`LinCertU.exists_dual`).
-/
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A59
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A61
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A67
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A91
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A95
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A111
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A117
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A123
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A135
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A147
import Chi2U.VOdd.CertData.A195

namespace Chi2U
namespace VOdd

/-- **Direct certificates** (PROOF_VODD §0, §3) at the 11 traces of `certA`, in the format of `DualCertU`. -/
theorem exists_certOdd_proof {a : ℕ} [Fact (1 ≤ a)] (ha : a ∈ certA) : ∃ C : DualCertU a, C.Phi ≤ PhiC a := by
  simp only [certA, Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at ha
  rcases ha with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
  · exact CertData.A59.cert
  · exact CertData.A61.cert
  · exact CertData.A67.cert
  · exact CertData.A91.cert
  · exact CertData.A95.cert
  · exact CertData.A111.cert
  · exact CertData.A117.cert
  · exact CertData.A123.cert
  · exact CertData.A135.cert
  · exact CertData.A147.cert
  · exact CertData.A195.cert

end VOdd
end Chi2U
